ath xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mo>&#176;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;(Assume concentration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Mn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> to be same on change in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math> concentration). The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is __________.</p><p>(Rounded off to the nearest integer)</p><p>[Given: <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>303</mn><mi>RT</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>059</mn></math>]</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "406987", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f3975"}, {"id": "ef4451", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f3976"}, {"id": "1cdb35", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f3977"}, {"id": "9e0e94", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f3978"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f3979", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df91"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4780"], "concepts": ["61489bb3f154cd4590457c66"], "question": {"text": "<p>For the disproportionation reaction&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8652;</mo><mi>Cu</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced></math> at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>,</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>ln</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>&nbsp; (where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> is the&nbsp;equilibrium constant) is _______<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Given <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>:</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><msub><mo>&#176;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>V</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>E</mi><msub><mo>&#176;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>Cu</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>52</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mfrac><mi>RT</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>025</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "40fb89", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f397a"}, {"id": "b77823", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f397b"}, {"id": "09b244", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f397c"}, {"id": "36d48f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f397d"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f397e", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df91"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4780"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b69"], "question": {"text": "The number of correct statements from the following is...........<br />A.&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi>cell</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;is an intensive parameter<br />B. A&nbsp;negative&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msup></math>&nbsp;means that the redox couple is a stronger reducing agent than the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>/</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;couple.<br />C. The amount of electricity required for oxidation or reduction depends on the stoichiometry of the electrode reaction.<br />D. The amount of chemical reaction which occurs at any electrode during electrolysis by a current is proportional to the quantity of electricity passed through the electrolyte."}, "options": [{"id": "05b74b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f397f"}, {"id": "a18242", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f3980"}, {"id": "028b0e", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f3981"}, {"id": "221d73", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f3982"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f3983", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df91"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4780"], "concepts": ["61489bb3f154cd4590457c66"], "question": {"text": "<p>For the given reactions</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Sn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>Sn</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Sn</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><mi>Sn</mi></math>&nbsp;the electrode potentials are ; <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><msup><mi>Sn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>Sn</mi></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>140</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><msup><mi>Sn</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>Sn</mi></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>010</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. The magnitude of standard electrode potential for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Sn</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>Sn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> i.e. <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><msup><mi>Sn</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>Sn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>&#176;</mo></msubsup></math> is____<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>(Nearest integer)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "16d9a5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f3984"}, {"id": "fc11c2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f3985"}, {"id": "d27e45", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f3986"}, {"id": "84aaa2", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f3987"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f3988", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df91"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4780"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b69"], "question": {"text": "<p>A metal surface of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>cm</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;area has to be coated with nickel layer of thickness <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>001</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mm</mi><mo>.</mo></math> A current of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> was passed through a solution of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ni</mi><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>NO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8216;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#8217;</mo></math> seconds to coat the desired layer. The value&nbsp;of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is _________. (Nearest integer)</p><p>(<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#961;Ni</mi></math>&nbsp;(density of Nickel) is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>10</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mL</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo></math>Molar mass of Nickel is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>60</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>96500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Cmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>)</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "3cc635", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f3989"}, {"id": "313f26", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f398a"}, {"id": "f5e3a4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f398b"}, {"id": "56d4f0", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f398c"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f398d", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df91"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4780"], "concepts": ["61489bb3f154cd4590457c66"], "question": {"text": "What would be the electrode potential for the given half-cell reaction at <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>?</mo><mi></mi><mo>_</mo><mo>_</mo><mo>_</mo><mo>_</mo><mo>_</mo><mo>_</mo><mo>_</mo><mo>_</mo><mo>_</mo><mo>.</mo></math><br /><math><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mover><mrow><mtext>H</mtext></mrow><mrow><mo>&#8853;</mo></mrow></mover><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup><mo>;</mo><msubsup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>1.23</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math><br /><math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8.314</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">l</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">T</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>298</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mo>;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">y</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r&#160;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">tan</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">dard&#160;</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>.</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">p</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">u</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">f</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow></mfenced></math>"}, "options": [{"id": "68e401", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f398e"}, {"id": "3cf0d8", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f398f"}, {"id": "1d0d92", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f3990"}, {"id": "e57588", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f3991"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f3992", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df91"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4780"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b69"], "question": {"text": "<p>A solution of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msub><mfenced><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></mfenced><mn>3</mn></msub></math> is electrolyzed for &#39;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math>&#39; min with a current of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>5</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> to deposit <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3482</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Fe</mi></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></math> is - [nearest integer]</p><p>Given : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>96500</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>Cmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>. Atomic mass of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Fe</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>56</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>gmol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "968603", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f3993"}, {"id": "8a02ee", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f3994"}, {"id": "e1243d", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f3995"}, {"id": "ae5622", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f3996"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f3997", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df91"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4780"], "concepts": ["61489bb3f154cd4590457c66"], "question": {"text": "The standard reduction potentials at \\(298 \\mathrm{~K}\\) for the following half cells are given below :\n\\(\\begin{array}{ll}\n\\mathrm{Cr}_2 \\mathrm{O}_7^{2-}+14 \\mathrm{H}^{+}+6 \\mathrm{e}^{-} \\rightarrow 2 \\mathrm{Cr}^{3+}+7 \\mathrm{H}_2 \\mathrm{O}, \\mathrm{E}^{\\circ}=1.33 \\mathrm{~V} \\\\\n\\mathrm{Fe}^{3+}(\\mathrm{aq})+3 \\mathrm{e}^{-} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Fe} \\qquad \\mathrm{E}^{\\circ}=-0.04 \\mathrm{~V} \\\\\n\\mathrm{Ni}^{2+}(\\mathrm{aq})+2 \\mathrm{e}^{-} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Ni} \\qquad \\mathrm{E}^{\\circ}=-0.25 \\mathrm{~V} \\\\\n\\mathrm{Ag}^{+}(\\mathrm{aq})+\\mathrm{e}^{-} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Ag} \\quad\\qquad \\mathrm{E}^{\\circ}=0.80 \\mathrm{~V} \\\\\n\\mathrm{Au}^{3+}(\\mathrm{aq})+3 \\mathrm{e}^{-} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{Au} \\qquad \\mathrm{E}^{\\circ}=1.40 \\mathrm{~V}\n\\end{array}\\)\nConsider the given electrochemical reactions,\nThe number of metal(s) which will be oxidized be \\(\\mathrm{Cr}_2 \\mathrm{O}_7^{2-}\\), in aqueous solution is ______"}, "options": [{"id": "800716", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f3998"}, {"id": "c015d5", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f3999"}, {"id": "8b7911", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f399a"}, {"id": "728be6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f399b"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f399c", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df91"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4780"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b69"], "question": {"text": "<p>Consider the following reaction</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>5</mn><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>-</mo></msup><mo>&#8594;</mo><msup><mi>Mn</mi><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>&#176;</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>51</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p>The quantity of electricity required in Faraday to reduce five moles of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>MnO</mi><mn>4</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math> is&nbsp;<u>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</u></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "209baa", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f399d"}, {"id": "a9d342", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f399e"}, {"id": "79d069", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f399f"}, {"id": "e69694", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39a0"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39a1", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df91"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4780"], "concepts": ["61489bb3f154cd4590457c66"], "question": {"text": "<p>In an electrochemical reaction of lead, at standard temperature, if&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>Pb</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>Pb</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mtext>&#160;Volt&#160;&#160;</mtext></math>and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>Pb</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>Pb</mi></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">n</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Volt</mi><mo>,</mo></math>then the value of&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mo>&#176;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msup><mi>Pb</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>Pb</mi><mrow><mn>4</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;&nbsp;is given by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8211;</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>xn</mi></math>. The value of x is _______. (Nearest integer)</p><p>&nbsp;</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "767847", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39a2"}, {"id": "5ae26a", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39a3"}, {"id": "e3f1ad", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39a4"}, {"id": "ad1c8c", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39a5"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39a6", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df91"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4780"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b69"], "question": {"text": "The amount of charge in <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math>&nbsp;(Faraday) required to obtain one mole of iron from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Fe</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math> is ______. (Round off the answer to the nearest integer)"}, "options": [{"id": "6565fb", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39a7"}, {"id": "01abaf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39a8"}, {"id": "dc840b", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39a9"}, {"id": "1c2656", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39aa"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39ab", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df91"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4780"], "concepts": ["61489bb3f154cd4590457c66"], "question": {"text": "<p>For the cell&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cu</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>1</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8214;</mo><msup><mi>Ag</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>01</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfenced><mi>Ag</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;the cell potential <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3095</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>.&nbsp;For the cell&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Cu</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi>Cu</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>01</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>&#8214;</mo><msup><mi>Ag</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>(</mo><mi>aq</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>001</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfenced><mi>Ag</mi><mo>(</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mo>)</mo></math>&nbsp;the cell potential <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>.</mo></math>&nbsp;Find value of x (Round off the Nearest Integer).</p><p>[ Use <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>:</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>303</mn><mi>RT</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>059</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi></math>&nbsp;]</p>"}, "options": [{"id": "1c6fe6", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39ac"}, {"id": "207ee7", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39ad"}, {"id": "eedecf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39ae"}, {"id": "f8d576", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39af"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39b0", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df91"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4780"], "concepts": ["60e56739499d1e49588f8b69"], "question": {"text": "The quantity of electricity in Faraday needed to reduce <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>mol</mi></math> of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Cr</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>7</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></mrow></msubsup></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>Cr</mi><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> is"}, "options": [{"id": "00de55", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39b1"}, {"id": "19f9cf", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39b2"}, {"id": "699c9f", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39b3"}, {"id": "78e1fa", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39b4"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39b5", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df91"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4780"], "concepts": ["61489bb3f154cd4590457c66"], "question": {"text": "<p>The equilibrium constant for the reaction <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Zn</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>Sn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mo>&#8652;</mo><msup><mi>Zn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mfenced><mi>aq</mi></mfenced><mo>+</mo><mi>Sn</mi><mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi></mfenced></math> is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>20</mn></msup></math> at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math>. The magnitude of standard electrode potential of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Sn</mi><mo>/</mo><msup><mi>Sn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup></math> if <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><msup><mi>Zn</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>*</mo></mrow></msup><mo>/</mo><mi>Zn</mi></mrow><mn>0</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>76</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> is _____ <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math>. (Nearest integer)</p><p>Given : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>303</mn><mi>RT</mi></mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>059</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p>"}, "options": [{"id": "3ab450", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39b6"}, {"id": "c8ca83", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39b7"}, {"id": "31c3a4", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39b8"}, {"id": "f83d32", "text": "", "isCorrect": null, "_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39b9"}], "questionLabels": []}, {"_id": "69de4f825dcf815cd79f39ba", "type": "numerical", "chapters": ["60c9e849ea076dc381c0df91"], "topics": ["60e2fada66f9ce3f243b4780"], "concepts": ["61489bb3f154cd4590457c66"], "question": {"text": "<p>The electrode potential of the following half cell at&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>298</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mfenced close=\"|\" open=\"|\"><mrow><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">X</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>001</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>&#8214;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></mrow></msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>01</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mfenced><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">Y</mi></math>&nbsp;is&nbsp;_____&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> (Nearest integer)</p><p>Given : <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsu